Z||000000||stimpy||05-09-2001||04:27 PM||||O.K. So my car has been having some drivability issues lately. It's been really lagging when it's cool, and ever really running as smoothly as it should even when warmed up. So we're thinking TPS. <P>On my way to the parts store, I'm accelerating out of a parking lot. I'm leaning on the gas and it doesn't want to get up and go. Suddenly the car bucks, I look in my rearview to see a HUGE puff of smoke! Funy thing isis the car suddenly LURCHES forward like I flipped nitrous on, theexhaust sounds throatier then I ever remembered, and the asthmatic wheeze from the intake is gone.<P>So what's the dilly-o? Was my cat plugged up and unplugged itself? (4 yo low restriction honeycomb cat) Do I need to be concerned? Or should I just sacrifice something to bring thanks to the Fiero gods?<BR>||||reg||4
